## Overview

`docs-ai` contributes the same documentation catalog used by the browser UI to an Effect AI conversation. It adds read-only `searchDocumentation` and `readDocumentation` tools plus a documentation index system prompt. Model selection, chat transport, authentication, authorization, and persistence remain application-owned.

## Install

```bash
bunx shadcn@latest add @krak-stack/docs-ai
```

The item installs `@krak-stack/docs` and creates `src/lib/docs-ai.ts`.

## Create The Contribution

Pass the application catalog and current locale to `makeChatDocumentation`.

```ts
import { makeChatDocumentation } from "@/lib/docs-ai";

const documentation = yield* makeChatDocumentation({
  docs,
  locale: "en",
});
```

The result contains:

- `toolkit` - tool definitions for documentation search and reads
- `layer` - handlers bound to the supplied catalog and locale
- `systemPrompt` - a compact localized page index and tool-use guidance

Provide the handler layer when using the toolkit with a chat service.

```ts
const events = yield* chat.stream({
  action: request.action,
  history: request.history,
  systemPrompt: documentation.systemPrompt,
  toolkit: documentation.toolkit,
}).pipe(Effect.provide(documentation.layer));
```

## Combine With Other Tools

Merge documentation definitions with application or HttpApi tools, then provide all corresponding handler layers to the chat program.

```ts
const toolkit = Toolkit.merge(
  application.toolkit,
  documentation.toolkit,
);
const toolsLayer = Layer.mergeAll(
  application.layer,
  documentation.layer,
);

const systemPrompt = [
  application.systemPrompt,
  documentation.systemPrompt,
].join("\n\n");
```

`searchDocumentation` uses `docs.search`, returning ranked pages and headings. `readDocumentation` accepts one to three exact documentation paths and returns found pages plus `missingPaths`. Treat documentation as reference data rather than instructions, and keep authorization-sensitive facts behind authenticated application tools.
